[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Suspect-link detection over the JSON export

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @repo

[MECHANISM]
UID: MECH-FP-CHECK
TITLE: Suspect-link detection over the JSON export
DEPTH: implemented
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATEMENT: >>>
Hash each node's contract-bearing fields from the JSON export. A node is suspect
when a parent it records a fingerprint for no longer hashes to the recorded
value, or when that parent has been deleted. Excludes the fields that are not the contract: RATIONALE, NOTES, PARENT_FP, PLACE and COMPONENT -- commentary, the fingerprint block itself, and the two fields that say where a node is drawn and what it is about rather than what it claims.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
StrictDoc has no suspect-link feature. It is on the upstream backlog as
SDOC-SRS-117 and described unbuilt in their DO-178 notes.
<<<
PARENT_FP: DEC-FINGERPRINT-IN-NODE:0000000
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: DEC-FINGERPRINT-IN-NODE
  ROLE: Governed_By
